# Shell scripts must always be checked out with LF endings. This repo is
# edited on Windows, but the *.sh scripts (backup.sh, restore.sh, …) run on
# the Linux VPS: a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for `/bin/sh\r` and
# fails with "bad interpreter". Forcing eol=lf means the server never needs a
# manual `sed -i 's/\r$//'` after a checkout or a tar|ssh ship.
*.sh text eol=lf
